      "x": -400,
      "y": -350,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 800,
      "color": "5",
      "label": "2. Sample Preparation"
    },
    {
      "id": "a1b2c3d4e5f60003",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -350,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 800,
      "color": "6",
      "label": "3. Labeling & Multiplexing"
    },
    {
      "id": "a1b2c3d4e5f60004",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 400,
      "y": -350,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 800,
      "color": "3",
      "label": "4. MS Acquisition"
    },
    {
      "id": "a1b2c3d4e5f60005",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 800,
      "y": -350,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 800,
      "color": "1",
      "label": "5. Data Analysis"
    },
    {
      "id": "a1b2c3d4e5f60011",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Cell Isolation Methods\n\n### FACS\n- High purity sorting\n- Live/dead selection\n- Surface markers\n\n### CellenONE\n- Image-based isolation\n- Direct dispensing\n- Size/morphology selection\n\n### Manual Picking\n- Micromanipulator\n- Limited throughput",
      "x": -780,
      "y": -310,
      "width": 310,
      "height": 300,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "a1b2c3d4e5f60012",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### Report Relevant Conditions\n\nRecord cell type, isolation strategy, recovery, viability criteria and contamination controls. Volumes and throughput depend on the specific platform and study; no universal values apply.",
      "x": -780,
      "y": 30,
      "width": 310,
      "height": 180
    },
    {
      "id": "a1b2c3d4e5f60013",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### Quality Controls\n\nUse controls appropriate to the sample and assay. Document cell selection, processing delays, blanks and technical variation. See the linked method notes and [reporting recommendations](https://doi.org/10.1038/s41592-023-01785-3).",
      "x": -780,
      "y": 250,
      "width": 310,
      "height": 170,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "a1b2c3d4e5f60021",
      "type": "file",
      "file": "notes/methods/SCoPE2.md",
      "x": -380,
      "y": -310,
      "width": 310,
      "height": 140
    },
    {
      "id": "a1b2c3d4e5f60022",
      "type": "file",
      "file": "notes/methods/nPOP.md",
      "x": -380,
      "y": -140,
      "width": 310,
      "height": 140
    },
    {
      "id": "a1b2c3d4e5f60023",
      "type": "file",
      "file": "notes/methods/nanoPOTS.md",
      "x": -380,
      "y": 30,
      "width": 310,
      "height": 140
    },
    {
      "id": "a1b2c3d4e5f60024",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### Method Comparison\n\n- [[mPOP]]: low-volume preparation\n- [[nPOP]]: nanoliter droplets on slides\n- [[nanoPOTS]]: nanowell-based preparation\n\nCompare equipment, sample compatibility, recovery and throughput using the original study conditions. Cost is not a fixed property of the method.",
      "x": -380,
      "y": 200,
      "width": 310,
      "height": 220,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "a1b2c3d4e5f60031",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## TMT/TMTpro (Isobaric)\n\nUsed in [[SCoPE2]] and [[pSCoPE]].\n\n- Reporter-ion quantification\n- Channel allocation depends on labeling chemistry\n- Carrier/reference channels are study-dependent\n- Interference can compress ratios\n\nUse the source protocol for the selected design.",
      "x": 20,
      "y": -310,
      "width": 310,
      "height": 220,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "a1b2c3d4e5f60032",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Non-isobaric Multiplexing\n\n[[plexDIA]] combines mass-offset labels and DIA.\n\n- Original study: 3-plex mTRAQ\n- Dimethyl and PSMtags: distinct later implementations\n- Precursor and fragment evidence support quantification\n\nLabeling and interference affect accuracy.",
      "x": 20,
      "y": -60,
      "width": 310,
      "height": 200,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "a1b2c3d4e5f60033",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Label-Free\n\n- No sample multiplexing label\n- Can use DDA or DIA\n- Separate acquisitions are generally required for separate samples\n\nWorkflow complexity and cost depend on the full experiment.",
      "x": 20,
      "y": 170,
      "width": 310,
      "height": 140,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "a1b2c3d4e5f60034",
      "type": "file",
      "file": "notes/methods/plexDIA.md",
      "x": 20,
      "y": 340,
      "width": 310,
      "height": 100
    },
    {
      "id": "a1b2c3d4e5f60041",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## DDA (Data-Dependent)\n\nSelects detected precursors for fragmentation. Used with both labeled and label-free samples. Selection and stochastic sampling affect completeness. See [[DDA]].",
      "x": 420,
      "y": -310,
      "width": 310,
      "height": 180,
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "a1b2c3d4e5f60042",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## DIA (Data-Independent)\n\nSamples predefined precursor windows. It does not guarantee fragmentation or detection of every peptide. Analysis can use empirical/predicted libraries or library-free workflows. See [[DIA]] and [[DIA-NN]].",
      "x": 420,
      "y": -100,
      "width": 310,
      "height": 180,
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "a1b2c3d4e5f60043",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Instrument Examples\n\n- Bruker timsTOF family\n- Thermo Orbitrap Astral / Exploris\n- Evosep LC workflows\n- IonOpticks columns\n\nInstrument, LC system and analytical column are distinct parts of the workflow.",
      "x": 420,
      "y": 110,
      "width": 310,
      "height": 200,
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "a1b2c3d4e5f60060",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Selecting a Workflow\n\nCompare sample type, available equipment, required multiplexing, protein coverage, quantitative reliability and total instrument time.\n\n[[SCoPE2]], [[plexDIA]], [[nPOP]], [[nanoPOTS]] and [[mPOP]] describe different stages or combinations; they are not mutually exclusive choices in a simple decision tree.",
      "x": -200,
      "y": 520,
      "width": 600,
      "height": 250,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "a1b2c3d4e5f60044",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### Acquisition Conditions\n\nGradient, flow, isolation windows and accumulation time must be taken from the chosen instrument/method. [[nDIA]] and [[Chip-Tip]] document different study-specific settings.",
      "x": 420,
      "y": 340,
      "width": 310,
      "height": 100
    },
    {
      "id": "a1b2c3d4e5f60051",
      "type": "file",
      "file": "notes/tools/MaxQuant.md",
      "x": 820,
      "y": -310,
      "width": 310,
      "height": 100
    },
    {
      "id": "a1b2c3d4e5f60052",
      "type": "file",
      "file": "notes/tools/DIA-NN.md",
      "x": 820,
      "y": -180,
      "width": 310,
      "height": 100
    },
    {
      "id": "a1b2c3d4e5f60053",
      "type": "file",
      "file": "notes/tools/scp Package.md",
      "x": 820,
      "y": -50,
      "width": 310,
      "height": 100
    },
    {
      "id": "a1b2c3d4e5f60054",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### Analysis Steps\n\n1. Identification and error control\n2. Quantification and QC\n3. Normalization appropriate to the design\n4. Batch assessment; correction only when justified\n5. Missingness assessment; imputation only with defensible assumptions\n6. Downstream analysis and validation",
      "x": 820,
      "y": 80,
      "width": 310,
      "height": 180,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "a1b2c3d4e5f60055",
      "type": "file",
      "file": "notes/tools/DO-MS.md",
      "x": 820,
      "y": 290,
      "width": 310,
      "height": 100
    },
    {
      "id": "a1b2c3d4e5f60010",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# SCP Methods & Workflows\n## From Sample to Data",
      "x": -125,
      "y": -680,
      "width": 700,
      "height": 100,
      "color": "1"
    }
  ],
